    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get that, but for the sake of the debate, I really need to go deeper into the actual \"evidence\" they present. Like, what specific concepts or historical arguments do they use to make their case sound scientifically plausible? For example, do they use things like brain size studies, specific evolutionary psychology theories, or certain types of population genetics data to justify these claims? Just trying to nail down the technical side of their rhetoric so I'm not caught off guard.",
